menu "HardID secure-element backend"

choice HARDID_SE_BACKEND
    prompt "SE backend for this build"
    default HARDID_SE_MOCK

config HARDID_SE_MOCK
    bool "Software mock (no secure-element hardware)"
    help
        Compile the in-RAM mock backend (core/se_mock.c). Used for bring-up,
        host tests and board bring-up when no ACL16 secure element is wired.
        Signatures are deterministic stand-ins (digest XOR seed) — fine for
        plumbing, NOT for real keys.

config HARDID_SE_ACL16
    bool "ACL16 dual secure element (SPI)"
    help
        Compile the production dual-ACL16 composite backend
        (hal/se_composite.c + se_acl16.c + se_transport_esp32*.c).
        Real ECDSA signing inside the SE. Requires two ACL16 parts on the
        board SPI pins (see hardware selection doc). When fitted this swaps
        the mock for real hardware-backed signing with zero changes to the
        UI/service layers.

endchoice

config HARDID_SE_ACL16_FULL
    bool "Build the ACL16 sources into the flash image"
    depends on HARDID_SE_BACKEND = "ACL16"
    default y
    help
        Pulls hal/se_composite.c, se_acl16.c and the SPI transport into the
        S3 build. Only meaningful when the ACL16 hardware is present.

endmenu

menu "HardID development options"

config HARDID_DEV_NO_PIN
    bool "Development: disable PIN prompts AND PIN gating"
    depends on HARDID_SE_MOCK
    default n
    help
        Bring-up convenience: skips every on-screen PIN prompt and treats
        the secure element as already unlocked. DEVELOPMENT ONLY — real
        devices must ship with this off. When enabled the sign/watch flows
        run without any PIN entry. Requires the mock SE backend.

endmenu